## Context

R10's present suite has a sound direct-network-attempt instrument but does not
faithfully or completely decide the promise. It rejects the expressly permitted
one-time model download, never drives a populated build carrying library text,
ignores non-resolver loopback relays, and reports `local-by-default` from a run
whose adapter discloses a non-default preinstalled runtime. The local-embedder
check also fails a target with no embedder, although absence alone does not make
text leave the machine.

This is the suite-orchestration ticket, not an implementation ticket. It owns
the child roster, sequencing, coverage reconciliation and final handoff. It owns
no ruling, assertion, adapter, sandbox mechanism, fixture or result artifact.
`SPEC.md` remains the authority for R10 and its named exception; the unresolved
choice already recorded in `DECISIONS.md` must be ruled before a child changes
what a red means.

## Children

- **0661 — reconcile egress grading with the permitted model download.** Obtain
  the pending ruling and make the executable clause match it without weakening
  coverage by accident.
- **0662 — trace populated build and the complete lifecycle.** Put real library
  text on every relevant default path and guard the path roster against omission.
- **0663 — detect exfiltration through local relays.** Close the loopback and
  Unix-socket forwarding false green with an end-to-end control.
- **0664 — measure the genuine default configuration.** Remove or separately
  classify harness-supplied runtime state and put the local-embedder mechanism
  check under the promise it actually establishes.

Children carry their own implementation, tests, evidence and machine-readable
dependencies. Work that is independent of the ruling in 0661 proceeds without
waiting for it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Children 0661–0664 exist and partition the missing suite.
- [ ] Each child closes with its own gates and evidence satisfied.
- [ ] The generated acceptance roster contains each resulting R10 check once
      and proves every relevant lifecycle path is assigned.
- [ ] README, SPEC.md, DECISIONS.md and committed real-target artifacts agree on
      which promise each check decides and on R10's standing.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass at master close.

## Invariants

- This ticket coordinates; children implement.
- One independently reviewable instrument or ruling consequence per child.
- A permitted call is not a red, an unfired detector is not a pass, and a local
  mechanism is not by itself proof of end-to-end custody.
